  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Primary Healthcare Services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to provide  primary healthcare services nationally access to quality primary healthcare services for underserved urban,
peri-urban and rural communities through the mobile clinics. The aim is to reach at least 500,000 patients by 2030.

Primary healthcare services to be provided include,
&#x2022; Curative care
&#x2022; Sexual Reproductive Health Rights (SRHR)
&#x2022; Provide mother to childcare
&#x2022; Dental health
&#x2022; HIV/AIDS treatment and care
&#x2022; Hypertension and Diabetes diagnosis and treatment
&#x2022; Pneumonia treatment
&#x2022; Antenatal care
&#x2022; Family planning
&#x2022; Early detection of chronic illnesses, i.e. PSA tests to detect prostate cancer
&#x2022; Vision Screening</narrative>
  </description>
